Background. A multi-normed space is a pair $((E^n,\|\cdot\|_n)_{n\in\mathbb N})$ consisting of a Banach space $E$ together with a sequence of norms $\|\cdot\|_n$ on the Cartesian powers $E^n$ satisfying the multi-norm axioms:
(A1) $\|(x_{\sigma(1)},\dots,x_{\sigma(n)})\|_n = \|(x_1,\dots,x_n)\|_n$ for every permutation $\sigma$;
(A2) $\|(\alpha_1 x_1,\dots,\alpha_n x_n)\|_n \le (\max_i |\alpha_i|)\,\|(x_1,\dots,x_n)\|_n$;
(A3) $\|(x_1,\dots,x_n,0)\|_{n+1} = \|(x_1,\dots,x_n)\|_n$;
(A4) $\|(x_1,\dots,x_n,x_n)\|_{n+1} = \|(x_1,\dots,x_n)\|_n$;
together with $\|x\|_1=\|x\|$.

For $p\in[1,\infty]$, a $p$-multi-norm is a multi-norm satisfying the additional homogeneity / averaging property characteristic of $\ell^p$-type behaviour, namely for all matrices $(a_{ij})$ with appropriate $\ell^p$-row/column conditions one has 
$$\Big\|\Big(\sum_j a_{1j}x_j,\dots,\sum_j a_{mj}x_j\Big)\Big\|_m \le \|a\|\cdot\|(x_1,\dots,x_n)\|_n,$$
where $\|a\|$ is the operator norm $\ell^p_n\to\ell^p_m$. A multi-norm is called $p$-convex (for $p\ge 1$) if $\|(x_1,\dots,x_n)\|_n \le (\sum_i\|x_i\|^p)^{1/p}$.

Operator sequence spaces (in the sense of Lambert) are Banach spaces $E$ equipped with a sequence of norms on $E^n$ arising from an embedding into a column-Hilbert-space-type structure; equivalently, a $2$-convex $2$-multi-norm coincides with an operator sequence space in this sense.

Problem. Identify which structural and representation-theoretic results known for operator sequence spaces (such as duality theory, characterizations via embeddings, tensor product constructions, and properties of multi-bounded maps between operator sequence spaces) admit suitable generalizations to $p$-multi-norms for general $p\in[1,\infty]$, and formulate and prove such generalizations.

